    "caveats": [
      "The registry resolves lymphatic endothelium to the HUVEC/microvascular entry; the 0.1–1 Pa shear there is the blood-vascular convention. For a lymphatic model we intentionally target 0.01 Pa (0.1 dyn/cm²), the low end of the lymphatic range — confirm the target against your lymphatic-specific literature (collecting lymphatics ≈ 0.1–1 dyn/cm²).",
      "Lymphatic shear is physiologically oscillatory/cyclic (valve-driven). This design delivers steady unidirectional flow; if you need the oscillatory component, add a pulsatile/rocking profile.",
      "0.4 µL/min is a very low flow — confirm your syringe pump holds stable flow at this rate and that the tubing/connectors do not leak at the ~4 Pa backpressure.",
      "Verify endothelial monolayer formation and junctional markers (e.g. LYVE-1, PROX1) rather than TEER, which is not a meaningful readout for this line.",
      "Seed ~1,200 cells on the 0.08 cm² floor; allow 24–48 h to reach confluence before starting perfusion."
    ]
  },
